course: dictionary
lesson: 4094
title: Gills: breathing in water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gill is a body part that lets an animal take oxygen out of water. We all need oxygen to live, and fish get it from water instead of air. «Fish take oxygen from water with gills.» So when you meet gill in a science text, think about breathing underwater.
explain: Gills are thin, feathery parts full of blood vessels. Water goes in through the mouth and comes out over the gills. «Out of water the gills collapse, so the fish cannot get oxygen.» That is why a fish lying on dry land cannot breathe for long.
explain: Gill has a second meaning. «Gills are also the thin lines under the cap of a mushroom.» Use the context to tell which one is meant: if the sentence talks about fish, water or oxygen, it means the breathing body part; if it talks about a mushroom or its cap, it means the thin lines.
fact: A gill is a body part that takes oxygen from water.
fact: Fish, tadpoles, crabs and sharks breathe with gills.
fact: Whales and dolphins are mammals, so they breathe air with lungs.
fact: «Gills» can also mean the thin lines under the cap of a mushroom.
fact: «Green around the gills» means looking sick.
exercise: «Fish take oxygen from water with gills.» What are gills? | Small fins that help the fish swim | *Body parts that take oxygen from water | Sharp teeth for catching food
exercise: Which animal breathes with lungs, not gills? | Crab | *Dolphin | Shark | Tadpole
exercise: «The gills under the mushroom cap were pale.» What does gills mean here? | Tiny feathers on a bird | *Thin lines under the cap of a mushroom | Body parts that take oxygen from water
test: «Water goes in through the mouth and out over the gills.» Where does the water leave a fish? | *Over the gills | Through the tail | Into the lungs | Back out of the mouth only
test: «Young amphibians usually live in water and breathe with gills.» What does usually mean? | Always, with no exceptions | Only in the summer | Never | *Most of the time, but not always
exam: Ruby reads, «The candiru is a tiny catfish that enters the gills of bigger fish.» What is the best way to work out what gills means? | Guess it is a type of fish | *Use the clues: a fish and blood, so gills are body parts for breathing | Skip the word and never think about it again | Look only at the word gill in a dictionary of mushrooms
